law.text:
		The provisions of this chapter shall be liberally construed so as to effectuate the following purposes:

To foster, encourage, and promote the safe and efficient exploration for and development, production, utilization, and conservation of the Commonwealth's gas and oil resources;


To provide a method of gas and oil conservation for maximizing exploration, development, production, and utilization of gas and oil resources;


To recognize and protect the rights of any person owning an interest in gas or oil resources contained within a pool;


To ensure the safe recovery of coal and other minerals;


To maximize the production and recovery of coal without substantially affecting the right of a gas or oil owner proposing to drill a gas or oil well to explore for and produce gas or oil;


To protect the citizens and the environment of the Commonwealth from the public safety and environmental risks associated with the development and production of gas or oil; and


To recognize that the use of the surface for gas or oil development shall be only the use that is reasonably necessary to obtain the gas or oil.
